SUMMARY:Hello Fall Colours: Dorset Hike & Lookout Tower
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/dorset-hike-and-lookout)**
 \n\n**Not every good trail makes it into a guidebook\, and this hidden gem
  sure hasn't.**\n\nTucked just southwest of Algonquin\, it's a route we ke
 ep close for our members: rolling rock outcrops\, quiet beaver ponds\, and
  wide ridges that open into sweeping views when you least expect them. In 
 September\, the whole forest turns to a radiant display of red\, orange\, 
 and gold\; the kind of colours that makes you stop mid-stride. Welcome to 
 fall in Ontario.\n\nWe'll cover 7.5 km at a comfortable pace\, with plenty
  of time to take it in before stopping for lunch at one of the best views 
 on the route. It's a moderate hike\, and a solid choice if this is your fi
 rst time out on trail.\n\nFrom the trailhead\, it's a short drive to Dorse
 t. The tower was first built in 1922 as a fire lookout and rebuilt in 1967
  into the structure that stands today. Climbing to the top puts you level 
 with the treetops and gives you a panorama of the hills and lakes around L
 ake of Bays\, all dressed in their fall colours. It's one of Ontario's mos
 t recognizable lookouts\, offering a totally different perspective after a
  morning spent within the tree canopy.\n\n**Please note that anyone not ta
 king the WU transportation will need to purchase their own tower access pa
 ss.**\n‍\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our
  adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodatio
 n request relating to a disability or provide feedback\, please do so by s
 ending an email to [info@wildernessunion.com](mailto:info@wildernessunion.
 com)\n\n**Highlights**\n**The Lookout Tower Climb:** The observation deck 
 sits 142 metres above Lake of Bays\, with a 360 degree view over the surro
 unding hills and lakes.\n**A Trail Off the Map:** A quiet\, little-known r
 oute kept for Wilderness Union members\, far from the lineups that build u
 p around Dorset in the fall.\n**Fall Colours:** Red\, orange\, and gold sc
 attered across the Canadian Shield.\n\n**Event cost: $75+HST (for explorer
  members) + $60 optional transport available.**\n**Register [here.](https:
 //www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/dorset-hike-and-lookout)**\n\n**About
  Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outd
 oors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoor
 s and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. T
 he group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canad
 a and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual eve
 nt attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. L
 arge enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's no
 t overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](
 https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316360117/
