SUMMARY:Fall Migration Birding in Toronto
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**To
 ronto has some hidden natural gems\, and October is when it puts on its be
 st show.**\n\nJoin our guide Pedro Hernandez of[ Outdoor Commute](https://
 www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) for a beginner-friendly birdwatching w
 alk through the unique Tommy Thompson Park. You do not need to know a warb
 ler from a wren\, but you probably will when the day is done. This walk is
  built for people who are simply curious about the birds sharing our skyli
 ne.\n\nWe’ll move slowly and stop often\, learning how to identify speci
 es by shape\, colour\, and call\, how to actually use a pair of binoculars
  (yours to borrow for the day)\, and how to make sense of field guides and
  birding apps you can keep using long after the trip ends.\n\nOctober is p
 eak Fall migration in the city\, with so many different birds to spot. Dep
 ending on conditions\, we might spot warblers\, sparrows\, and thrushes mo
 ving through\, along with waterfowl like northern shovelers and gadwalls r
 esting on the water. Year-round residents including red-tailed hawks\, bla
 ck-capped chickadees\, and northern cardinals tend to make an appearance t
 oo.\n\n**Please note that binoculars are included in the cost of the adven
 ture and that\, due to the Toronto location\, transportation is not offere
 d.**\n\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adv
 entures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation re
 quest relating to a disability or provide feedback\, please do so by sendi
 ng an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Fall Migratio
 n:** October is one of the best windows of the year to bird at the Spit\, 
 with local species and southbound migrants both moving through the park at
  once.\n**Professional Birder:** Pedro founded the popular birding account
 [ Outdoor Commute](https://www.instagram.com/outdoor.commute/) and brings 
 a genuine\, patient teaching style\n**Binoculars Included:** Every partici
 pant gets a pair of high-quality NOCS binoculars for the walk\n\n**Event c
 ost: $60+HST (for explorer members). Register [here.](https://www.wilderne
 ssunion.com/adventures/fall-birding-26)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nW
 ilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that co
 nnects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find y
 our people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of G
 TA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAtten
 dance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typ
 ically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there
 's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***
 Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wilderness
 union.com/)***
