SUMMARY:Group Camping at Killbear
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/camping-killbear)**\n\n**J
 oin us for a fall camping trip at the famous Killbear Provincial Park!**\n
 \nWe're spending one night during peak fall colours at Killbear's group si
 tes\, tucked into the pines a short walk from Georgian Bay's beaches. This
  site offers all of the conveniences of front country camping. It's a good
  entry point if you've never spent a night outside the city\, and a good r
 eset if you have.\n\nDay one will include a short hike along the beach in 
 Parry Sound\, arrival at camp\, camp setup and exploration. Once tents are
  up and the site is sorted\, the afternoon is easy: a walk down to the bea
 ch to take in the shoreline\, a few camp skills to pick up around the site
 \, and time to just hang out before dinner. As the sun starts to drop\, an
 d if the weather smiles down upon us\, we will head to Sunset Rock togethe
 r\, where Killbear's famous windswept pine has been holding its ground on 
 bare granite for decades. It's one of the most photographed sunsets on the
  peninsula\, and it's even better in person.\n\nDay two starts with the Lo
 okout Point Trail\, a moderate \\~6km climb through hardwood forest of ash
 \, beech\, oak\, and maple to a granite lookout with sweeping views across
  the Bay's 30\,000 Islands.From there it's back to camp to pack up and hea
 d back to Toronto.\n\nYou'll leave with sand in your shoes and a crew you 
 didn't have two days ago.\n\nWhat's included\n\n* Professional & certified
  guides\n* ‍All camp meals\, cooking equipment and mess kits\n* ‍Tents
 \n\nSleeping bags and sleep pads can be rented from WU for a small fee.\n\
 n**Accessibility**\n\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventur
 es as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request
